      "properties": {
        "entityId": "tang",
        "startDate": "0781-01-01",
        "endDate": "0782-11-30",
        "order": 19,
        "segmentType": "other",
        "name": {
          "zh": "幽州—莫州—魏州（朱滔南下）",
          "en": "Youzhou–Mozhou–Weizhou (Zhu Tao moves south)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "建中二年（781）正月成德节度使李宝臣死，其子李惟岳求袭不允，与魏博田悦、淄青李正己连兵拒命。朝廷诏幽州留后朱滔讨李惟岳，朱滔自幽州出兵，军于莫州，与张孝忠破李惟岳于束鹿，进围深州。建中三年（782）朝廷割深州与康日知，朱滔求深州不得而怨，遂应田悦之邀反唐，六月率幽州兵南下，至魏州惬山与官军交战，十月在魏州西郊称冀王。原线只有幽州—魏州两点、日期作 781 全年，线头无前置；此处补莫州、改起止日期并写明两段。路线为示意。",
          "en": "In the first month of 781 Li Baochen of Chengde died and his son Li Weiyue was refused hereditary succession, so he joined Tian Yue of Weibo and Li Zhengji of Ziqing in revolt. The court ordered Zhu Tao, acting governor of Youzhou, to attack Li Weiyue; Zhu Tao marched from Youzhou, camped at Mozhou, defeated Li Weiyue at Shulu with Zhang Xiaozhong and besieged Shenzhou. In 782 the court gave Shenzhou to Kang Rizhi; Zhu Tao, denied it, turned against the court at Tian Yue’s invitation, marched south in the sixth month and fought the imperial army at Qieshan near Weizhou, taking the title of Prince of Ji in the tenth month. The former line had only two points and a whole-year date of 781 with no precedent at its head; Mozhou is added and the two phases are now described. The line is schematic."
        },
        "extensions": {
          "precision": "schematic"
        }
      }
