        "name": {
          "zh": "洛阳—涿郡（永济渠）",
          "en": "Luoyang–Zhuojun (Yongji canal)"
        },
        "description": {
          "zh": "大业四年（608）正月，炀帝“将兴辽东之役，自洛口开渠达于涿郡，以通漕”，发河北诸郡男女百余万开永济渠，引沁水南达于河，北通涿郡，全长二千余里。此渠把军粮与将士运至东北前线，为 612 年征辽东的准备；原数据中涿郡—辽东段的线头因此有来由。路线为示意，馆陶、沧州等经行点只入正文。",
          "en": "In the first month of 608, preparing the Liaodong campaign, Emperor Yang had the Yongji canal dug from the Luo mouth to Zhuojun “for transport”, mobilising over a million men from Hebei to lead the Qin river south to the Yellow River and north to Zhuojun, over 2,000 li. The canal carried troops and grain to the north-eastern front and prepares the 612 Liaodong campaign, giving the Zhuojun–Liaodong route its head. The line is schematic; Guantao and Cangzhou appear only in the text."
        },
